# The build context is apps/worker/sandbox — build.sh resolves HERE to this
# directory and passes it as the context (build.sh:28, build.sh:45). A
# .dockerignore is resolved relative to the CONTEXT ROOT, so this file has to
# live here; one at the repository root would do nothing at all.
#
# THIS IS A CREDENTIAL GUARD, NOT A BUILD OPTIMISATION.
#
# `.build-secrets` sits in this directory (mode 0600) and holds the real
# MONOREPO_PAT and NUCLEO_LICENSE_KEY. Both are supposed to reach the build
# ONLY through BuildKit `--secret` mounts (id=monorepo_pat,
# id=nucleo_license_key), which never become a layer and never show up in
# `docker history`. Without this file they are still uploaded to the Docker
# daemon as ordinary build context — one `COPY . .` away from being baked into
# a layer that gets pushed to a registry.
#
# build.sh already greps `docker history` and the assembled filesystem for both
# values after every build. This is the guard that stops them entering in the
# first place.
.build-secrets
.build-secrets.*
!.build-secrets.example

# Not consumed by the image. The Dockerfile COPYs exactly two paths —
# provision.sh (Dockerfile:273) and harness/record.cjs (Dockerfile:278) — so
# nothing excluded here is needed by the build.
build.sh
*.md

# Never present in this directory today, but cheap insurance if the context
# ever widens.
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.env
**/*.env
**/.dev.vars
**/.DS_Store
